KG42.register("clusters-5106297ece19f5238222c55d",{"id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v142-d-K002","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","label":"Autonomous participation and trading choices within an allocated DOE.","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Autonomous participation and trading choices within an allocated DOE.","market_meaning":"With the already allocated DOE as an external condition, prosumers and the consumer role within them may participate in local trading within the limit and, through buy/sell bids, choose P2P or upper-grid trading; the statement that the DSO does not explicitly participate in price settlement retains its original scope.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01-doe","v141-a-M02-prosumer-energy-management","v141-a-M03-lem"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"M01 provides the background of DOE-constrained participation, and M03 provides participation permission and trading-channel choice; the consumer classification of M02 serves only as shared context, and it is not asserted on that basis that positive net power is a market-entry threshold, nor are net power and DOE treated as the same quantity.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"This cluster forms a procedural rule around what trading choices participants have within a given limit; DOE calculation, specific bid optimization, and price formation each have independent decision boundaries.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Retain the explanation of participation within the limit under the DOE mechanism, and do not expand it into a delivered network-computation chain."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Specify the consumer side's permission to participate in trading within the allocated DOE."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Specify autonomous participation, the choice between P2P and grid channels, and the procedural meaning of realizing the choice through bids."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"shared","role":"context","rationale":"Only explain the existing classification context of the consumer role; the primary attribution is in v142-d-K001, and it is not treated as a newly added access dependency of this cluster."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E27"],"rationale":"The former explains the network-constraint background for participation within the DOE limit, and the latter explains autonomous trading choice under the same framework; they are complementary only in scope and do not add a scientific edge between the DSO and the LMO."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E27"],"rationale":"The consumer-side permission is complementary to the prosumer's general participation choice; retain the consumer sub-scope and do not treat the two permission statements as completely duplicate."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"shared_node","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::participation.consumer"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::V::participation.consumer"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g02-E28"],"rationale":"The two chains reference the same frozen consumer node but respectively carry the explanation of operating-role classification and trading permission; this connection records only the reference identity and does not infer that the classification condition is a necessary condition for participation permission."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::participation.prosumer","v141-c-R008::V::participation.prosumer"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::V::participation.prosumer","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E27"],"rationale":"The two references have the same frozen node identity; the representative item is used only for display, and the DOE background of M01 and the participation choice of M03 remain separately traceable."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::participation.consumer","v141-c-R007::V::participation.consumer"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R007::V::participation.consumer","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g02-E28"],"rationale":"Unify the display reference for the same frozen node; do not merge the constraints of consumer determination and participation permission, and do not eliminate the difference in scope between the two mechanisms."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"Participation permission, role context, and DOE background all come from B evidence that has not been independently verified; the source status remains unverified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E28"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually verify the permission wording, the scope of actors, and the original qualification that the DSO does not explicitly participate in price settlement; no claim may be made on that basis that an independent source audit has been completed."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G02","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"It remains unclear whether the consumer wording in R007 strictly refers to the time-varying set defined in R002; identical node identity is insufficient to establish a mapping of eligibility conditions.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g02-E28"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Confirm the scope of the consumer term in the two mechanisms; if a conditional relation from role to permission is to be established, explicit support should be supplied separately, and for now the shared context is maintained."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"This cluster takes the already allocated DOE as a condition; the frozen chain does not provide a complete representation of DOE calculation and network-security verification, the related node proposals remain unapproved, and an access node or LMO node cannot be used as a substitute.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E27"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-doe","proposal:v141-b-g02-P01","v141-b-g03-p01-doe","v141-b-g03-p04-network-security-validation"],"required_work":"If extending to DOE generation or network verification, the corresponding chain should be completed upstream and the proposal handled manually; currently no new node is inserted, nor is procedural participation permission treated as proof of network-security calculation."}]},"rule_refs":["43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R001","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R007","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R008","43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R002"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-440139830bbd658e","COMP-49b8505fe0a8fb55","COMP-4fd16cbd90d234cb","COMP-a774da994c2ca212"]});
